What is someone to do? And I love that the psalmists are not trying to disguise that.

134
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:20,400
They're not trying to hide it. They're not trying to make it cliche or sound like, "Man, if you would just get up out of your chair

135
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:25,400
and move towards God, everything would be great." You guys heard those sermons? Turn them off.

136
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:35,400
Moving towards God's presence in the midst of a broken world, you will face the valley of Baca.

137
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:45,400
You're gonna have to go through it. You're gonna have to suffer. You're gonna doubt.

138
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:55,400
But you have to keep moving towards Him. Because eventually, your weeping will turn to rejoicing.

139
00:27:55,400 --> 00:28:03,400
And eventually, you will begin to see that the storms in your life will actually produce a harvest of God's goodness if you will allow it.

140
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:07,400
And this is why it's so important that we do this thing together in community.

141
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:13,400
Because not all of us are in the same place at the same time, and those of us who are in the midst of the valley of Baca

142
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:18,400
and need those of us who have come through the valley of Baca and on the other side so that we can cheer to you.

143
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:26,400
Keep going. Keep your head up. Keep moving forward. Keep setting your eyes on God's presence, on His dwelling place.

144
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:32,400
Because I know it's hard. I know it doesn't make sense. I know none of it. None of it seems to be working out.

145
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:38,400
And yet better is one day in the courts of the Lord than thousands else.

146
00:28:39,400 --> 00:28:52,400
As they pass through the valley of Baca, they make it the place of springs. The autumn rain covers it with pools.

147
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:57,400
They go from strength to strength till each appears before God in Zion.

148
00:28:57,400 --> 00:29:03,400
I don't know about you, but when is the last time you took a long, difficult journey where you went from strength to strength?

149
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:08,400
Is that the natural way that we go on long, difficult journeys?

150
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:15,400
I just played nine holes at Rock Harbor a couple weeks ago. It was right before a storm.

151
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:23,400
I walked nine, which, you know, that's a sacrifice. This course has like 600 feet of elevation change.

152
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:28,400
I was trying to beat the storm, so the first hole, I sprinted from my shot to my shot to my shot.

153
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:35,400
The second hole, I kind of sprinted from my shot to my shot to my shot. The third hole, it turned into a jog.

154
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:41,400
The fourth hole into a power walk. The fifth hole into a walk, walk.

155
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:46,400
And nothing about my journey could be defined as moving from strength to strength.

156
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:54,400
It was all moving from strength to weakness. Till the very end, I was like dragging myself up a hill,

157
00:29:54,400 --> 00:30:01,400
thinking why in the world do people do this for fun? This is not fun. This is why they made carts.

158
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:06,400
They made carts so that we could ride in them. This is, what are we doing?

159
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:12,400
Anyway, that was a silly illustration to say that difficult journeys lead us from strength to weakness.

160
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:17,400
So what is it that the psalmist is saying that when we get up and we start journeying through the valley of suffering,

161
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:24,400
through the valley of pain, what is it about this journey towards God's presence that leads us from strength to strength?

162
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:30,400
It doesn't make sense. But the reason that as we journey towards God,

163
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:42,400
that we gain strength rather than losing strength, is because the end destination becomes clearer to us the closer we get to God's presence.

164
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:49,400
And the end destination for those who are journeying towards God is new creation, is resurrection.

165
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:54,400
It's not just redemption in this life, but it's redemption in the life to come.

166
00:30:54,400 --> 00:31:01,400
It's that we realize that our life is but a vapor here on earth, and yet God is worried about eternity.

167
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:13,400
That God's redemption, that his reconciliation isn't just about healing us here on earth, but it's about restoring all of creation back to himself moving forward.

168
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:19,400
And that's the picture of the temple, the tabernacle. It was this temporary thing that was to remind them of what was to come,

169
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:24,400
that ultimately God's presence wouldn't be locked in one geographic location for one specific people,

170
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:31,400
but that it was gonna blow up and go to all the world, that God would bless all of the world through the people of Israel.

171
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:38,400
And the reason that we can go from strength to strength as new covenant people, when we're suffering, when we're struggling,

172
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:44,400
when we're wrestling, is because the closer we get to God, the more that we realize that God is more worried about

173
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:51,400
ultimate eternal reconciliation and redemption than just this life.

174
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:58,400
And I know it doesn't always make sense, because this is the life that we experience here and now.

175
00:31:58,400 --> 00:32:08,400
But as the destination of God's redemptive plan comes clear into focus, we begin to move from strength to strength to strength.

176
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:17,400
And I've got a friend, a close friend who I've had the privilege of walking with in the midst of turmoil and difficulty and struggle.

177
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:32,400
A friend who has lost unexpectedly. A friend who had every reason to say, "Nah, man. I'm good. I'm good with the God thing."

178
00:32:32,400 --> 00:33:00,400
Like, I've given my life to him. And this is how I get treated. And yet, as I've journeyed with that friend and as they've gotten a more concrete vision for God's eternal redemption, his eternal reconciliation, that his plan is ultimately about resurrection, is about bringing death to life, is about bringing the brokenness of this fallen temporary place to a ultimate conclusion through the resurrection of Jesus.

179
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:21,400
As they've come into clarity for that, I've seen them move from strength to strength. I've seen, and it's not ignoring the suffering. It's not, oh, I'm blessed and highly favored. It's this is hard, but God is good. This is death, but God is life.

180
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:48,400
This is lost, but God is, He is resurrecting. He is restoring. He is redeeming. And that is how we can move from strength to strength as we get into picture, a clearer vision of what God is ultimately doing in our lives. And it's far less about the 50, 60, 70 years that we have here on earth, and it's far more about the eternal weight of His glory.

181
00:33:48,400 --> 00:34:00,400
Okay. Verses eight and nine, the weird interlude. It's a petition. It's a prayer that doesn't make sense to new covenant people, so I'm not going to spend a whole lot of time on it, but I do want to make it make sense.

182
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:15,400
It's the only time the psalmist pray for anything specifically. And that, I want to, when we talk about prayer as Christians, 90% of the things that we mean is us asking God to do something for us and for others.

183
00:34:15,400 --> 00:34:24,400
Read the Psalms. That's not what prayer is completely. God's welcoming our complaints. He's welcoming our wrestling. Prayer is interacting with God.

184
00:34:24,400 --> 00:34:34,400
And so we don't have to come to Him and ask for something all the time. Totally fine. We're invited to do that, but that's not the only thing that is defined as prayer.

185
00:34:34,400 --> 00:34:42,400
But this is the only thing the psalmist asks for. They say, "Hear my prayer, Lord God Almighty. Listen to me, God of Jacob. Look on our shield, O God.

